SDL2_mixer 2.6.3: mixing without an SDL audio device (RISC OS)

Mix_OpenAudioExternal() sets the mixer up without opening an SDL audio
device, and Mix_MixAudioExternal() mixes the next block on request, from
any thread; Mix_LockAudio() then uses a mutex of the mixer's own. On RISC
OS the program feeds SharedSoundBuffer itself, from whichever of its
threads gets time, instead of depending on one SDL audio thread that
UnixLib's scheduler may not run for a while.

--- a/include/SDL_mixer.h
+++ b/include/SDL_mixer.h
@@ -458,6 +458,23 @@
